BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 678 Tm (1. Check group descriptor and bitmap bounds before trusting an inode number. A plausible) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 661.5 Tm (superblock does not make every group readable.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 635 Tm (2. Reject directory entries with zero progress, invalid record sizes or inode references) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 618.5 Tm (outside the recorded inode population.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 592 Tm (3. Validate indirect block levels and detect loops, duplicate block ownership and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 575.5 Tm (pointers outside the volume; corrupted trees must not trigger infinite traversal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 549 Tm (4. Cross-check inode link counts with directory references and allocated data blocks with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 532.5 Tm (the block bitmap. Disagreements require diagnosis, not automatic rewriting.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 506 Tm (5. Respect clean-state and error flags. A volume modified without journaling may need a) Tj ET
